{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T636QoKZFRQW4xYCm94VMQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Gandalf Runtime Host (Tier-1 deterministic) — Description (Foreman intake)\n2\t\n3\t## What is being built\n4\tThe **missing runtime host** for the shipped Gandalf v1 skill — the \"thin runtime entry\" the build log\n5\trecords as an open follow-up (`../crucible-advisor/EXECUTION-LOG.md`, `LESSONS.md`, `journal/0001`). It takes\n6\ta live Gandalf analysis's **RAW draft** (the model's un-stamped findings/elevations/diagnosis, per\n7\t`SKILL.md §RUNTIME`) and runs it through the **already-shipped deterministic seam engine** (`seam/*.mjs`) to\n8\tproduce a **canary-conformant, honestly-graded** advisor output (`schema/advisor-output.schema.json`),\n9\tvalidated by the **already-shipped** `test/harness.mjs assertIncrement1Conformant`.\n10\t\n11\tThis makes Gandalf's grades **real and deterministic** instead of model-self-asserted (the authors' first\n12\treal run showed the model \"keeps hand-approximating tier stamps and failing the canary\" without this host).\n13\t\n14\t## Scope = Tier 1 (deterministic), by design\n15\t- The host runs the **deterministic** seam pass on ONE model run. It does **NOT** dispatch the live\n16\t  independent named-defeater refuters or the researchPrime SITUATE commission (that needs the `agent()`\n17\t  seam the repo flags as \"the integration point the gate never runs\" — `seam/refute.mjs:26-28`).\n18\t- Therefore every **elevation** honestly lands at **SPECULATIVE** carrying the\n19\t  `NO_INDEPENDENT_REFUTATION_STAMP` (\"no independent refutation ran\") — the seam's own honest floor\n20\t  (`vetElevationRefutation` / `stampNoIndependentRefutation`). The **diagnosis** findings keep their evidence\n21\t  rungs and `gandalf_core` provenance; `risk_labels` are capped at the single-family **PROMISING** ceiling\n22\t  (`composeRiskLabels`, `cross_model:false`). Only **REFUTED** drops (`dropsFromOutput`).\n23\t- The live-refuter PROMISING tier is a **sequenced follow-on** (it needs the `agent()` seam), consistent with\n24\t  the Gandalf program's own dependency sequencing. **Not in this effort.**\n25\t\n26\t## Reuses (does NOT fork) the shipped engine\n27\t`seam/refute.mjs` (`vetElevationRefutation`, `stampNoIndependentRefutation`, `firesRefuter`,\n28\t`SPECULATIVE_TIER`, `NO_INDEPENDENT_REFUTATION_STAMP`), `seam/score-label.mjs` (`labelTier`,\n29\t`composeRiskLabels`, `dropsFromOutput`, `scoreDualAxis`), `seam/diagnose-core.mjs`\n30\t(`stampDiagnoseCoreProvenance`), `seam/anticipate.mjs` (`composeAnticipation`), `seam/situate.mjs`\n31\t(`composeSituate`), `test/harness.mjs` (`assertIncrement1Conformant`, `validateShape`). The host adds glue +\n32\ta CLI entry; it invents no new grading logic.\n33\t\n34\t## Done-floor + gate discipline (PRINCIPLE-D, unchanged)\n35\tGround-truth gate = the deterministic `node --test test/*.test.mjs` (the existing 130 canary tests + the new\n36\thost tests). The live-refuter `agent()` dispatch is OUT of scope and OUT of the gate. Single-family →\n37\t`cross_model:false`. No npm deps (Node 20+; the repo uses `import ... with { type: 'json' }`).\n38\t\n39\t## Non-negotiables\n40\t- Reuse the shipped seams; never reimplement grading. Never weaken/skip the existing 130 canary tests.\n41\t- A malformed/partial raw draft → an HONEST named error (no fabricated finding, no forged conformant output).\n42\t- Every elevation is SPECULATIVE + stamped (no over-claim); the top-level owns any degradation (B6); only\n43\t  REFUTED drops. The host output passes `assertIncrement1Conformant` by construction.\n44\t- Additive only: a new `runtime/` dir + new `test/runtime-*.test.mjs` + a documentation touch to `SKILL.md`\n45\t  §RUNTIME / `LESSONS.md` / `journal/`. No unrelated repo files touched.\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"665cab02-cdc0-4e90-964f-140d19967d66","uuid":"8fcd6aa3-de96-460a-bf4a-eeb7c53abb72","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:22:54.877Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\skills\\gandalf\\planning\\runtime-host\\DESCRIPTION.md","content":"# Gandalf Runtime Host (Tier-1 deterministic) — Description (Foreman intake)\n\n## What is being built\nThe **missing runtime host** for the shipped Gandalf v1 skill — the \"thin runtime entry\" the build log\nrecords as an open follow-up (`../crucible-advisor/EXECUTION-LOG.md`, `LESSONS.md`, `journal/0001`). It takes\na live Gandalf analysis's **RAW draft** (the model's un-stamped findings/elevations/diagnosis, per\n`SKILL.md §RUNTIME`) and runs it through the **already-shipped deterministic seam engine** (`seam/*.mjs`) to\nproduce a **canary-conformant, honestly-graded** advisor output (`schema/advisor-output.schema.json`),\nvalidated by the **already-shipped** `test/harness.mjs assertIncrement1Conformant`.\n\nThis makes Gandalf's grades **real and deterministic** instead of model-self-asserted (the authors' first\nreal run showed the model \"keeps hand-approximating tier stamps and failing the canary\" without this host).\n\n## Scope = Tier 1 (deterministic), by design\n- The host runs the **deterministic** seam pass on ONE model run. It does **NOT** dispatch the live\n  independent named-defeater refuters or the researchPrime SITUATE commission (that needs the `agent()`\n  seam the repo flags as \"the integration point the gate never runs\" — `seam/refute.mjs:26-28`).\n- Therefore every **elevation** honestly lands at **SPECULATIVE** carrying the\n  `NO_INDEPENDENT_REFUTATION_STAMP` (\"no independent refutation ran\") — the seam's own honest floor\n  (`vetElevationRefutation` / `stampNoIndependentRefutation`). The **diagnosis** findings keep their evidence\n  rungs and `gandalf_core` provenance; `risk_labels` are capped at the single-family **PROMISING** ceiling\n  (`composeRiskLabels`, `cross_model:false`). Only **REFUTED** drops (`dropsFromOutput`).\n- The live-refuter PROMISING tier is a **sequenced follow-on** (it needs the `agent()` seam), consistent with\n  the Gandalf program's own dependency sequencing. **Not in this effort.**\n\n## Reuses (does NOT fork) the shipped engine\n`seam/refute.mjs` (`vetElevationRefutation`, `stampNoIndependentRefutation`, `firesRefuter`,\n`SPECULATIVE_TIER`, `NO_INDEPENDENT_REFUTATION_STAMP`), `seam/score-label.mjs` (`labelTier`,\n`composeRiskLabels`, `dropsFromOutput`, `scoreDualAxis`), `seam/diagnose-core.mjs`\n(`stampDiagnoseCoreProvenance`), `seam/anticipate.mjs` (`composeAnticipation`), `seam/situate.mjs`\n(`composeSituate`), `test/harness.mjs` (`assertIncrement1Conformant`, `validateShape`). The host adds glue +\na CLI entry; it invents no new grading logic.\n\n## Done-floor + gate discipline (PRINCIPLE-D, unchanged)\nGround-truth gate = the deterministic `node --test test/*.test.mjs` (the existing 130 canary tests + the new\nhost tests). The live-refuter `agent()` dispatch is OUT of scope and OUT of the gate. Single-family →\n`cross_model:false`. No npm deps (Node 20+; the repo uses `import ... with { type: 'json' }`).\n\n## Non-negotiables\n- Reuse the shipped seams; never reimplement grading. Never weaken/skip the existing 130 canary tests.\n- A malformed/partial raw draft → an HONEST named error (no fabricated finding, no forged conformant output).\n- Every elevation is SPECULATIVE + stamped (no over-claim); the top-level owns any degradation (B6); only\n  REFUTED drops. The host output passes `assertIncrement1Conformant` by construction.\n- Additive only: a new `runtime/` dir + new `test/runtime-*.test.mjs` + a documentation touch to `SKILL.md`\n  §RUNTIME / `LESSONS.md` / `journal/`. No unrelated repo files touched.\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}}}
